      "amount": "1 teaspoon",
      "notes": "for cheesy, nutty flavor"
    },
    {
      "name": "salt",
      "amount": "1 teaspoon",
      "notes": "to enhance flavors"
    },
    {
      "name": "black pepper",
      "amount": "1/2 teaspoon",
      "notes": "to enhance flavors"
    }
  ],
  "instructions": [
    "Sous-vide cook the collard greens at 90\u0002f for 2 hours.",
    "Heat 1 tablespoon of olive oil in a large pan over medium heat.",
    "Add the chopped onion and saut\u00185n until translucent, about 5 minutes.",
    "Add the minced garlic and cook for 1 minute, until fragrant.",
    "Add the caramelized onion mixture to the cooked collard greens.",
    "Stir in the nutritional yeast, salt, and black pepper.",
    "Transfer the mixture to a serving dish and drizzle with the remaining 1 tablespoon of olive oil and 1 tablespoon of apple cider vinegar.",
    "Garnish with fresh spruce tips, if desired.",
    "Serve warm, with a side of whole grain bread or over quinoa, if desired."
